    plain: {
      zh: "須菩提再度提起開篇雙問：發菩提心者云何應住、云何降伏其心？問題重提，表示聽眾已走過前半經的離相訓練，可以承受更徹底的答案。佛陀重申：當生如是心——我應滅度一切眾生；滅度一切眾生已，而無有一眾生實滅度者。若菩薩有我相、人相、眾生相、壽者相，則非菩薩。所以者何？「實無有法，發阿耨多羅三藐三菩提心者」——連「發心」本身也無固定之法可執；發心是運心趨向覺悟與利他，不是獲得一張「菩提心證書」。再勘驗：如來於燃燈佛所，有法得無上正覺不？須菩提答：如我解佛所說義，佛於燃燈佛所，無有法得阿耨多羅三藐三菩提。度生的悲願不減，對能度、所度、所得的執取卻要徹底掏空——這才是中段對「住」與「降伏」的究竟安立。",
      en: "Subhūti raises again the opening twin questions: how should one who has set the mind on awakening abide, and how subdue the mind? Restating them signals that hearers, trained in freedom from marks through the first half, can bear a more thorough answer. The Buddha restates: give rise to this thought — I should liberate all beings; yet having done so, in truth not one being has been liberated. If a bodhisattva holds notions of self, person, being, or life span, that one is not a bodhisattva. Why? “In truth there is no dharma called setting the mind on supreme perfect awakening” — even “aspiration” is not a fixed thing to grasp; aspiring is turning the mind toward awakening and altruism, not obtaining a certificate of bodhicitta. He examines again: at Dīpaṃkara Buddha’s place, did the Tathāgata attain any dharma of supreme awakening? Subhūti answers that, as he understands, there was no dharma of attaining. The compassionate vow to liberate does not shrink, while grasping at liberator, liberated, and attainment must be emptied thoroughly — that is the mid-sutra’s ultimate grounding of abiding and subduing."
    },
